Backport of upstream's repeated-string-instruction series (Paolo Bonzini,
2024-12-15, merged for QEMU 10.0) plus its two follow-ups, applied in
upstream order without conflicts:
  6ace2d5163bb inline gen_jcc into sole caller
  e604be4fb4ed remove trailing 1 from gen_{j,cmov,set}cc1
  b519556f58dc unify REP and REPZ/REPNZ generation
  d8d552d45912 unify choice between single and repeated string instructions
  0eb7046e1bbe reorganize ops emitted by do_gen_rep, drop repz_opt
  4d7704ebc59a tcg: move gen_set/reset_* earlier in the file
  0d82d9e84644 fix RF handling for string instructions
  6986cf003226 make cc_op handling more explicit for repeated string instructions
  365811602572 do not use gen_op_jz_ecx for repeated string operations
  0360b781870a optimize CX handling in repeated string operations
  456709db50f4 execute multiple REP/REPZ iterations without leaving TB
  4f094e27f3ad pull computation of string update value out of loop
  82290c764760 extract common bits of gen_repz/gen_repz_nz
  22063f03a762 avoid using s->tmp0 for add to implicit registers
Our x87-shadow.c.inc follows the gen_setcc1 -> gen_setcc rename.
Measured with tools/string-bench.py (DOS, TCG, x86-64 host): rep movsd /
movsb / stosb / stosd 12-16 % faster per element, repne scasb unchanged;
also brings translate.c closer to 10.x for later backports. Drop when the
base moves past QEMU 10.0.

